#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186347753 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "60e28b26-0eb7-51ed-bcf9-2660b98a6028" :knowledge-point/title "Finding a Tangent Line to a Curve"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "cbd9cf26-36a3-573f-be14-4292f29ef821" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨3,-1⟩+u⟨1,5⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186347755} {:answer/id #uuid "19c9af6e-fd42-5fe8-a8a0-4ef5c76c9b79" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨5,1⟩+u⟨3,0⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186347756} {:answer/id #uuid "d79405e0-cf4f-56f0-ba10-aaf9cddf88c4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨5,1⟩+u⟨3,-3⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186347757} {:answer/id #uuid "4d3f6f05-e2b9-5329-9364-d0192d174f99" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨3,-1⟩+u⟨3,0⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186347758} {:answer/id #uuid "0d66860a-50b2-5812-a611-399d148a0e71" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨5,1⟩+u⟨1,5⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186347759}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "19c9af6e-fd42-5fe8-a8a0-4ef5c76c9b79" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨5,1⟩+u⟨3,0⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186347756} :answer-field/id #uuid "cfba4061-161c-5e71-9c8e-3ddfb8354902" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186347754}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "28b07468-67e6-5160-b480-58f04dacf3f5" :question/math-academy-id "q-126835" :question/problem "Which of the following gives the equation of the tangent to the curve $r(t)=⟨3t+5,1-{t}^{3}⟩$ at the point where $t=0,$  valid for all  real values of $u?$" :question/worked-solution "At the point where $t=0,$ the vector ${r}^{′}(0)$ is tangent to the curve, so the tangent line to the curve at $P$ can be parametrized as\n \n\n$$\nR(u)=r(0)+u{r}^{′}(0),\\,u\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )\n$$\n\n \n\nFirst, we find $r(0):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r(0) & =⟨3(0)+5,1-{0}^{3}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨5,1⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n   \n\nNow, we calculate ${r}^{′}(t):$ \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(t) & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(3t+5),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(1-{t}^{3})⟩ \\\\  & =⟨3,-3{t}^{2}⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we evaluate ${r}^{′}(t)$ at $t=0:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(0) & =⟨3,-3(0)^{2}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨3,0⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, the tangent line to the given curve at the point where $t=0$ is\n\n$$\nR(u)=⟨5,1⟩+u⟨3,0⟩,\\,u\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).\n$$"}]}
